Simple Icons (https://simpleicons.org), version 16.35.0: alibabacloud.svg, betterstack.svg, braintrust.svg,
calendly.svg, convex.svg, duckdb.svg, excalidraw.svg, greenhouse.svg, hubspot.svg, kagi.svg, lottiefiles.svg, lucid.svg,
mixpanel.svg, nextdotjs.svg, sanity.svg, semrush.svg, shadcnui.svg, socket.svg, stripe.svg, webflow.svg, wix.svg,
zapier.svg. gilbarbara/logos draws these brands as a wordmark alone, too small to read in a tile, or not at all, or
(Next.js) with an element that may reach past the file, so each keeps Simple Icons' symbol: the icon's path alone, with
the brand's colour as the file's fill. DuckDB's is filled black instead, as its yellow (FFF000) does not show on the
white tile.

The marks are trademarks of their owners. Dot shows each to identify the service it stands for, and nothing more; its
use implies no endorsement. The owners' brand guidelines, where Simple Icons names them:

